## Concrete ownership

The request slot is independent from the AsyncWrap native slot and attaches before the genuine AsyncWrap constructor. The default SimpleShutdown owns only its own native state. The FileHandle variant adds real canonical filesystem request storage and actual ReqWrap Entry; its stream pointer is borrowed. It creates no handle Global, Promise, replacement queue, or synthesized native completion.

FileHandle shutdown uses the existing real Controller.dispatchRawClose and callback Wrapper. Completion performs trace end, actual AfterClose, a fresh result read, native cleanup, and Done. A completed ordinary callback exception does not skip the original native continuation. Scope retirement restores the trigger before releasing the outer request pointer and local handles. The real callback Wrapper remains alive through Done/Dispose.

The reusable reporter is native_node_stream_shutdown.reportAfterRequest(listener, request, status), with reportAfterShutdown as its typed adapter. This is the original ReportWritesToJSStreamListener body: disabled-JS return, actual arguments, optional error/ClearError, genuine Has.FromJust terminal policy, ordinary Get, nonfunction -> undefined, then actual MakeCallback. Generic StreamListener predecessor forwarding remains separate.

## Latin-1 scope

JS_PiNewStringLatin1 calls the real QuickJS one-byte allocator and preserves each input byte as the corresponding code unit. Explicit lengths preserve embedded NUL; negative signed lengths call actual strlen. The selected wrapper keeps the distinct explicit-over-max ToLocalChecked path and inferred-length internal MaybeHandle CHECK path, real allocation-failure ownership, and genuine native diagnostics.

The raw VM primitive does not implement V8's heap layout, one-character cache, or GC/retry machinery. Original length-zero and length-one factory decisions are recorded explicitly; no claim equates a QuickJS raw allocation with the full V8 heap policy. Internalized-string mode is outside this selected wrapper.

The build recipe compiles one TLS implementation, one V8 fatal owner and the new two-entry diagnostic adapter per new executable. The selected network library contains none of those three translation units. Neither DEBUG nor OFFICIAL_BUILD is selected, even when Zig optimize is Debug; native Debug/official parity is not claimed. Both C ABI entries install borrowed DiagnosticContextScope first and queue no context pointer.

